<h2 id="h-long-term-reliability-and-ownership">Long-Term Reliability and Ownership</h2>
<p>A compound bow lasts as long as you look after it. To keep a Lift 29.5 shooting the way it did on day one:</p>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Wax the string and cables</strong> regularly, especially after wet hunts.</li>
  <li><strong>Inspect the serving</strong> around the cams and the center serving for fraying or separation.</li>
  <li><strong>Check limb bolts and accessory screws</strong> before each season.</li>
  <li><strong>Store it in a case</strong> away from heat, such as a hot vehicle.</li>
  <li><strong>Have a pro shop check timing</strong> and replace strings when they show wear.</li>
</ol>
<p>Draw length changes on the Lift are made in half-inch steps. If you are not comfortable working on cams, let a Mathews dealer handle it. They can also confirm draw weight on a scale afterward.</p>
<?= callout('warn', 'Buying used?', 'Ask for the original draw length, draw weight class and let-off setting, check the serial number with a dealer, and inspect limbs for cracks or splinters. Factor in the cost of a new string set if the history is unknown.') ?>

